","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-04-13T16:52:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T14:30:45Z","closed_at":"2025-04-16T14:29:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nFound the issue in 4.4-beta2\nReproducible in 4.5-dev2, 4.4-beta2, 4.3-stable, 4.0-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev2.mono - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6614) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen getting the Size property of a NinePatchRect that is a child of a Container, the value returned seems to be based on the PatchMargin rather than the node's bounding rectangle. I found this issue using C# but I have also tested in gdscript and I get the same results.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a Container. (Doesn't seem to matter what kind of Container)\n2. Create a NinePatchRect as a child of the Container.\n3. Set the PatchMargin attribute.\n4. Attach the following script to the NinePatchRect:\n```gdscript\nextends NinePatchRect\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Size of NinePatchRect: %s\" % size)\n}\n```\n5. Run the scene and the printed size should reflect the PatchMargin rather than the node's bounding rectangle.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[ninepatchrectbug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19726306/ninepatchrectbug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"StarboiHooch","id":122087848,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0bpqA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122087848?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/S